            <ArticleTitle>Clinical experiences with colonoscopy. A review of 100 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>408-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Our experience with 100 colonoscopic examinations are described. The clinical value of the procedure is outlined and the minimal degree of attendant morbidity, when performed by a competent endoscopist, are emphasized. The indications and contraindications for this relatively recently devised diagnostic and therapeutic modality should be commonly known. The procedure should be done whenever indicated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
